# Fleet Builder Fix-Findings Prompt
File: openOODA/scripts/fleet/prompts/fix-findings.oot

Provenance: converted from openOODA/scripts/fleet/prompts/fix-findings.md (30 lines). Every
instruction, command, and finding slot is preserved. The WIP branch namespace is now the
generic `wip/fleet-<host>-<pane>` form.

Your last batch in {{REPO_PATH}} did not pass the review gate. Fix these findings.

REPO:   {{REPO_PATH}}
BRANCH: refs/heads/wip/fleet-$(hostname -s)-{{PANE}}

FINDINGS
========
{{FINDINGS}}

HOW TO FIX
  1. cd {{REPO_PATH}}
  2. Read each finding. Verify it against the source before changing anything - a finding
     that does not reproduce is not a defect. If you believe a finding is wrong, say so
     explicitly in your report and leave that code unchanged.
  3. Fix the real defects. Keep every page inside the Page Rule: 16-256 lines per file,
     <=8 functions per page, <=40 lines per function, <=8 pages per directory, and the
     4-element Academy header. Run lint-oo-size -> 0 violations.
  4. Do NOT push to master/main yet. Commit and push your fix to the WIP branch only:
         git add <explicit paths> && git commit -m "fix(review): <short description>" && \
         git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/wip/fleet-$(hostname -s)-{{PANE}}
  5. Re-run the gate:
         export OODA_COMPILER=/Projects/openOODA-core/oodac/bin/oodac.real
         export OODA_NO_JAIL=1
         export OO_LIST_AMBIENT_QUOTA=8589934592
         make verify && make test      # TWICE, byte-identical post-build output
  6. PROVE: git status -s empty, git rev-parse HEAD equals origin/master and origin/main.

REPORT: a table of finding -> fixed / not-a-defect (with the reason) -> commit sha -> gate result.
This is attempt {{ATTEMPT}} of a maximum of 3. After 3 failed attempts this repo is parked
and escalated, so be precise rather than broad.
